  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA-2000) achieves 48.5% acc, while config_010 (image-only, ResNet50, singleprofile) achieves only 20.8% acc, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. However, we have no evidence yet on whether the multiprofile setting (with aggregation) improves upon the single-profile baseline. Question: config_002 tests the same PCA-2000 RNA encoder under multiprofile with average-pool aggregation, isolating the effect of the profile/aggregation axis while holding the encoder constant. Why this is the best next experiment: The profile setting is a fundamental architectural decision that gates whether aggregation is needed at all and interacts with every downstream choice (encoder, fusion, image modality). Testing it first with the simplest aggregation (avgpool) and the already-validated PCA encoder gives a clean, interpretable signal. If multiprofile+avgpool improves on 48.5%, we gain a strong exploitation direction (try transformer aggregation, better encoders, multimodal fusion). If it does not, we can deprioritize the multiprofile axis and focus budget on encoder quality or fusion. This single experiment reduces the most critical uncertainty in the design space under a tight budget."
}

